From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 01:09:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tolerate identical duplicate op and kernel registrations

The same op/kernel registration TUs can be loaded twice into one process
(e.g. on macOS when a custom-op library such as the TFLite audio
microfrontend is loaded), so identical entries reach the process-global
registries a second time.

OpRegistry: In the systemlib build, both libtensorflow_framework.so and
libtensorflow_cc.so embed the same op-registration TUs (e.g.
function_ops.cc's _Arg), so OpRegistry's deferred queue gets two identical
entries and the first ProcessRegistrations() aborts with AlreadyExistsError
at `import tensorflow`. Make RegisterAlreadyLocked silently accept (and skip
the watcher callback for) a duplicate whose OpDef matches via OpDefEqual; a
divergent OpDef for the same name still errors.

OpKernel registry: In the systemlib build the same kernel-registration TU is embedded in both
libtensorflow_framework.so and libtensorflow_cc.so (both loaded at import),
so identical kernels such as _Send/_Recv register twice in the process-global
registry. On a GPU host the first host<->device copy then aborts with
"Multiple OpKernel registrations match NodeDef at the same priority"
(GPU-less CI never exercises this). Skip an exact-duplicate registration
(same key, kernel_class_name and serialized KernelDef) in
OpKernelRegistrar::InitInternal; genuinely distinct kernels are still added.
Mirrors the OpRegistry/PlatformObjectRegistry duplicate-tolerance patches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/tensorflow/core/framework/op.cc b/tensorflow/core/framework/op.cc
index 7688578d..6afe25ad 100644
--- a/tensorflow/core/framework/op.cc
+++ b/tensorflow/core/framework/op.cc
@@ -239,10 +239,41 @@ absl::Status OpRegistry::RegisterAlreadyLocked(
   if (s.ok()) {
     s = ValidateOpDef(op_reg_data->op_def);
   }
-  if (s.ok() &&
-      !registry_.try_emplace(op_reg_data->op_def.name(), std::move(op_reg_data))
-           .second) {
-    s = errors::AlreadyExists("Op with name ", op_reg_data->op_def.name());
+  // conda-forge tensorflow-feedstock: tolerate duplicate op registrations
+  // when the OpDef being re-registered is identical to the one already in
+  // the registry. With conda's systemlib build a process can load multiple
+  // TF shared objects (libtensorflow_framework.so.2, libtensorflow_cc.so.2,
+  // the _pywrap_*.so python extensions, and load_op_library() custom-op
+  // .so's) which each statically embed the same built-in op-registration
+  // translation units (e.g. function_ops.cc's REGISTER_SYSTEM_OP("_Arg")).
+  // Without this guard the second .so to register a built-in op causes
+  // ProcessRegistrations() to return AlreadyExistsError, surfaced from
+  // TF_LoadLibrary(_audio_microfrontend_op.so) during `import tensorflow`.
+  // Identical duplicates are silently accepted AND silently swallowed --
+  // the watcher (used by LoadDynamicLibrary to harvest the OpDefs registered
+  // by a newly-loaded custom-op .so) is not invoked for an accepted
+  // duplicate, so the duplicate built-in op is NOT mis-attributed to the
+  // custom library. A divergent OpDef for the same name still errors as
+  // before and is reported through the watcher.
+  bool silently_accepted_duplicate = false;
+  if (s.ok()) {
+    auto it = registry_.find(op_reg_data->op_def.name());
+    if (it != registry_.end()) {
+      if (OpDefEqual(op_reg_data->op_def, it->second->op_def)) {
+        silently_accepted_duplicate = true;
+      } else {
+        s = errors::AlreadyExists("Op with name ", op_reg_data->op_def.name());
+      }
+    } else {
+      registry_.try_emplace(op_reg_data->op_def.name(),
+                            std::move(op_reg_data));
+    }
+  }
+  if (silently_accepted_duplicate) {
+    // Skip the watcher: the duplicate's OpDef is identical to the one
+    // already registered and is NOT a definition contributed by the
+    // currently-loading custom op .so.
+    return absl::OkStatus();
   }
   absl::Status watcher_status = s;
   if (watcher_) {
--- a/tensorflow/core/framework/op_kernel.cc
+++ b/tensorflow/core/framework/op_kernel.cc
@@ -1359,6 +1359,21 @@
   auto global_registry =
       reinterpret_cast<KernelRegistry*>(GlobalKernelRegistry());
   mutex_lock l(global_registry->mu);
+  // conda-forge: in the systemlib build the same kernel-registration TU is
+  // embedded in more than one loaded TF .so (libtensorflow_framework.so and
+  // libtensorflow_cc.so), so identical kernels (e.g. _Send/_Recv) register
+  // twice in this process-global registry and FindKernelRegistration then
+  // aborts on a GPU host with "Multiple OpKernel registrations match ... at
+  // the same priority". Skip an exact duplicate (same key, class name and
+  // KernelDef); genuinely distinct kernels for the op are still added.
+  auto existing = global_registry->registry.equal_range(key);
+  for (auto it = existing.first; it != existing.second; ++it) {
+    if (it->second.kernel_class_name == kernel_class_name &&
+        it->second.def.SerializeAsString() == kernel_def->SerializeAsString()) {
+      delete kernel_def;
+      return;
+    }
+  }
   global_registry->registry.emplace(
       key,
       KernelRegistration(*kernel_def, kernel_class_name, std::move(factory)));
